KG42.register("rules-cc0770acb97d101429847c5b",{"id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R019","paper":"05-double_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R019","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M04","name":"Social-welfare clearing objective","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"TR's restriction of trading counterparties prevents social-welfare maximization because buyer gamma and seller gamma are excluded. Scope: Trade Reduction auction's selection of permitted trading buyers and sellers. Condition: Trades are limited to gamma minus one buyers and sellers, excluding buyer gamma and seller gamma.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.social_welfare under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.social_welfare","matching.counterparties"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R019-E001","source":"matching.counterparties","target":"clearing.social_welfare","type":"limits","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R019-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Trade Reduction auction's selection of permitted trading buyers and sellers.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"theta_gamma","symbol":"\\gamma","meaning":"Index of the marginal breakeven buyer-seller pair in the ordered offers; TR permits only \\gamma - 1 buyers and \\gamma - 1 sellers, so buyer \\gamma and seller \\gamma are excluded.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R019-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"TR's restriction of trading counterparties prevents social-welfare maximization because buyer gamma and seller gamma are excluded. Scope: Trade Reduction auction's selection of permitted trading buyers and sellers. Condition: Trades are limited to gamma minus one buyers and sellers, excluding buyer gamma and seller gamma.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R019-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"In the Trade Reduction auction, trades are limited to \\gamma - 1 buyers and \\gamma - 1 sellers; buyer \\gamma and seller \\gamma are not permitted to participate. Scope: Trade Reduction auction's selection of permitted trading buyers and sellers. Condition: The marginal breakeven index \\gamma is determined by the ordered offers.","expression":"\\#\\{\\text{permitted buyers}\\} = \\gamma - 1 \\;\\land\\; \\#\\{\\text{permitted sellers}\\} = \\gamma - 1 \\;\\land\\; \\text{excluded buyer index} = \\gamma \\;\\land\\; \\text{excluded seller index} = \\gamma","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_gamma"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-08","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M04-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"of trades while maintaining truthful bidding by limiting trades to 1 Ta buyers and sellers [45]. Suc","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The Trade Reduction (TR) auction mechanism avoids subsidization of trades while maintaining truthful bidding by limiting trades to $\\gamma - 1$ buyers and sellers [45]. Such differs from uniform k-DA and VCG, where $\\gamma$ buyers and sellers are allowed to transact. Because buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$ are not permitted to participate in the TR auction, social welfare is not maximized. However, trading buyers pay $B_{\\gamma}^P$ and trading sellers receive $S_{\\gamma}^P$. As $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P$, the market operator may financially gain $B_{\\gamma}^P - S_{\\gamma}^P$ from each single unit transaction."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"The rule's evidence (v141-b-g01-ev-08) states a mechanism-level restriction and its welfare consequence; it does not define a design-selection or operational decision variable controlled by this rule. \\gamma is a marginal index parameter, not a decision variable.","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M04-clearing","v141-a-M04-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.social_welfare","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-08","quote":"The Trade Reduction (TR) auction mechanism avoids subsidization of trades while maintaining truthful bidding by limiting trades to $\\gamma - 1$ buyers and sellers [45]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-08","quote":"Because buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$ are not permitted to participate in the TR auction, social welfare is not maximized."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"5e84a6821a13f97ae7c2c3408972c2ee8990d84d8d1ccab9d657c5d092f2573e","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The rule's explicit quantitative TR restriction can be formalized: evidence v141-b-g01-ev-08 states that TR limits trades to gamma - 1 buyers and gamma - 1 sellers and excludes buyer gamma and seller gamma, captured in supporting constraint C002. However, the core C001 claim that this prevents social-welfare maximization cannot be given a faithful mathematical expression from the frozen graph and this rule's evidence alone: ev-08 does not define a social-welfare function, individual utilities, participant sets, or the precise welfare objective, and the graph contains only clearing.social_welfare and matching.counterparties. C002 is an equivalent_translation of the source's prose count/exclusion statement, justified because it introduces no new numeric value, domain, or coefficient; gamma is the source's marginal index. B evidence v141-b-g01-ev-08 is unreviewed in this experiment, so no source-correctness claim is made. Revision is needed to add the welfare definition and index/set structure.","bindings":[{"object_id":"theta_gamma","node_ids":["matching.counterparties"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R019-E001"],"rationale":"\\gamma determines which marginal buyer and seller are excluded from matching.counterparties; that exclusion is recorded by edge E001 as limiting clearing.social_welfare."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R019-C001","node_ids":["matching.counterparties","clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R019-E001"],"rationale":"The core logical constraint states that TR's restriction on permitted counterparties prevents social-welfare maximization, corresponding to E001's limits edge from matching.counterparties to clearing.social_welfare."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R019-C002","node_ids":["matching.counterparties"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R019-E001"],"rationale":"The count/exclusion restriction is imposed on matching.counterparties; edge E001 links this restriction to the clearing.social_welfare objective."}],"revision_requests":["Request C.1 to extract and verify the source definition of social welfare/economic efficiency for the TR claim (e.g., the sum of individual utilities such that no participant is precluded from trading), with same-mechanism evidence, so C001's 'social welfare is not maximized' can be formalized.","Request C.1 to extract the ordered buyer and seller index sets and the definition of \\gamma as the marginal breakeven index, with evidence, so that 'buyer \\gamma', 'seller \\gamma', and the \\gamma - 1 permitted sets are typed as indices/sets rather than only as an informal symbol.","Request B re-extraction/audit for v141-b-g01-ev-08: the evidence is currently unverified and no independent source review has passed; confirm whether the source supplies a formal social-welfare or economic-efficiency expression and whether the TR exclusion of buyer \\gamma and seller \\gamma is tied to it.","If the TR operator surplus (B_{\\gamma}^P - S_{\\gamma}^P) is intended within this rule's welfare analysis, request C.1 to add the relevant pricing.local/settlement.payment nodes and evidence; otherwise that fact should remain in the separate payment and operator-surplus rules."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
